\tab(Ruby,
The binding is generated by Rosetta; the report shell puts the nix-built
`datamunge.rb` and its native extension on `RUBYLIB`. Vectors are Arrays:

```{ruby, nix-shell="git+file:../../../..#report-ruby", file="figures/plot_ruby.svg"}
require "fileutils"
require "datamunge"

def doppler(x) = x.map { |xi| Math.sin(20 / (xi + 0.25)) }

Datamunge.set_seed(42)
x = Datamunge.runif(0, 1, 1000)
y = doppler(x).zip(Datamunge.rnorm(0, 1, 1000)).map { |f, e| f + e }
xseq = Datamunge.seql(0, 1, 1000)
yseq = doppler(xseq)
yfit = Datamunge::BSplineRegression.new(x, y, 100).predict(xseq)
FileUtils.mkdir_p("build")
Datamunge::RPlot.create
  .title("Doppler data")
  .points(x, y, "Samples", Datamunge::RGB.new("#edc78799"))
  .lines(xseq, yseq, "True Mean", Datamunge::RGB.new("#c80a2c"), 3.0)
  .lines(xseq, yfit, "Estimated Mean", Datamunge::RGB.new("#2c0ac8"), 3.0)
  .x_label("X").y_label("doppler(X)")
  .size(1000, 600)
  .save("build/plot_ruby.svg")
```
