> Verification scope

All original language programs and their native package-shell selection are
retained. The relative Git-flake reference now resolves from this report
directory to the repository root. The C++ diagram uses the working-tree
pkg-config selection during batch verification. All sixteen language
package-shell programs passed actual execution.

The shared ten-document batch passes the native regression, sanitizer,
documentation and installed-header gates. All seventeen programs and their saved
native SVGs pass execution and both HTML and Markdown export checks.

> Verification and binding conventions

All seventeen complete programs execute: the introductory native C++ diagram and
sixteen original language examples. R uses R6 `$new()` constructors. JavaScript
vectors are ordinary arrays and Lua vectors are ordinary one-based tables. Each
language uses its Nix report shell and saves a local SVG. The language packages
share the canonical native fit and renderer; independently seeded language
random generators need not produce the same samples or fitted curve. The first
run builds missing packages; later runs reuse them. Actual execution receipts
and both document exports are retained under
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-284-293/plot/`.
